# The known differences between the present website and the generated static site, read by tools/site-compare.cs.
# One a line: page | kind | reason. A * in the page stands for any text. Kinds: status, title, heading, intro,
# list-missing, list-extra, list-title, list-order, main-text, reference-comma.
# Only a difference that was seen in a run, understood and accepted belongs here; anything else is a finding to decide on.
/articles/* | reference-comma | Decided 16 Nov 2026: the present site adds a comma after a page reference at a line end; the article's source has none, so the static site shows the source
/articles/*%* | status | Decided 16 Nov 2026: the present site answers 404 for an article whose slug is percent-encoded; the static site serves it
